<blockquote>
<p>All other texts referencing SCP-2383 are to be destroyed violently</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Violently? Is there a standard procedure to destroy them? From how it's presented, it feels like one can destroy via any means (be it excessive or &quot;not enough&quot;).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>is to be counted and replace</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;replace&quot; –&gt; &quot;replaced&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>some text concerning SCP-2383 is still, albeit very rarely, found in locations,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't really understand this portion's syntax. What are these locations? I know that those further apart are affected less. But I'm not sure what the quoted statement is trying to convey.</p>
<p>Unless it's part of the anomalous effect?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Pros:</p>
<ul>
<li>It's fairly meta. However, unlike other forms of meta SCPs, this one is relatively subtle and <em>can</em> pass off as a normal text.</li>
